btw NOERR:
btw Section 7 parameters. AMBIG-n comments mark readings of unclear spec text.

cook boom() { yeet "boom ran" }

btw ---- defaults
cook pair(a, b = 2) { itsgiving [a, b] }
yap pair(1)                              btw OUT: [1, 2]
yap pair(1, 9)                           btw OUT: [1, 9]
tryna { pair() } caught4k e { yap "err" }          btw OUT: err
tryna { pair(1, 2, 3) } caught4k e { yap "err" }   btw OUT: err

btw defaults see earlier parameters
cook earlier(a, b = a + 1, c = a + b) { itsgiving [a, b, c] }
yap earlier(1)                           btw OUT: [1, 2, 3]
yap earlier(1, 5)                        btw OUT: [1, 5, 6]
yap earlier(1, 5, 9)                     btw OUT: [1, 5, 9]
cook onlyearlier(a = b, b = 1) { itsgiving a }
tryna { onlyearlier() } caught4k e { yap "err" }   btw OUT: err
yap onlyearlier(7)                       btw OUT: 7
yap onlyearlier(7, 8)                    btw OUT: 7

btw a default expression is a full expression and stops at the comma
cook fancy(a, b = nocap ? 1 : 2, c = npc ?? 3) { itsgiving [a, b, c] }
yap fancy(0)                             btw OUT: [0, 1, 3]
cook closes(a, g = () => a) { itsgiving g() }
yap closes(3)                            btw OUT: 3

btw evaluated at each call, so a mutable default is fresh every time
cook fresh(xs = []) {
    slide(xs, 1)
    itsgiving xs
}
yap fresh(), fresh()                     btw OUT: [1] [1]
lowkey base = 1
cook readbase(a = base) { itsgiving a }
base = 2
yap readbase()                           btw OUT: 2

btw AMBIG-11: "evaluated at each call" read as: only when the argument is omitted
lowkey calls = 0
cook bump() {
    calls += 1
    itsgiving calls
}
cook counted(a = bump()) { itsgiving a }
yap counted(), counted(), calls          btw OUT: 1 2 2
yap counted(100), calls                  btw OUT: 100 2
btw AMBIG-12: an explicit npc counts as passing the argument
yap counted(npc), calls                  btw OUT: npc 2
cook deferred(a = boom()) { itsgiving a }
yap deferred(5)                          btw OUT: 5
tryna { deferred() } caught4k e { yap e }    btw OUT: boom ran

btw defaults also work on lambdas
lowkey lam = cook(a, b = a * 2) { itsgiving a + b }
yap lam(2), lam(2, 1)                    btw OUT: 6 3

btw ---- rest
cook resty(a, ...rest) { itsgiving [a, rest] }
yap resty(1)                             btw OUT: [1, []]
yap resty(1, 2, 3)                       btw OUT: [1, [2, 3]]
tryna { resty() } caught4k e { yap "err" }         btw OUT: err
cook allof(...xs) { itsgiving clout(xs) }
yap allof()                              btw OUT: 0
yap allof(1, 2)                          btw OUT: 2
yap allof(...[1, 2, 3], 4)               btw OUT: 4

cook mixed(a, b = 2, ...rest) { itsgiving [a, b, rest] }
yap mixed(1)                             btw OUT: [1, 2, []]
yap mixed(1, 5)                          btw OUT: [1, 5, []]
yap mixed(1, 5, 6, 7)                    btw OUT: [1, 5, [6, 7]]
yap mixed(...[1, 2, 3])                  btw OUT: [1, 2, [3]]
yap mixed(1, npc, 3)                     btw OUT: [1, npc, [3]]
tryna { mixed() } caught4k e { yap "err" }         btw OUT: err

btw the rest list is new, it doesn't alias the spread source
lowkey spreadsrc = [1, 2]
cook grows(...r) {
    slide(r, 9)
    itsgiving r
}
yap grows(...spreadsrc), spreadsrc       btw OUT: [1, 2, 9] [1, 2]

btw ---- arity errors elsewhere
lowkey one = x => x
tryna { one() } caught4k e { yap "err" }           btw OUT: err
tryna { one(1, 2) } caught4k e { yap "err" }       btw OUT: err
lowkey two = (a, b) => a
tryna { two(1) } caught4k e { yap "err" }          btw OUT: err
lowkey none = () => 1
tryna { none(1) } caught4k e { yap "err" }         btw OUT: err
tryna { lam() } caught4k e { yap "err" }           btw OUT: err
tryna { lam(1, 2, 3) } caught4k e { yap "err" }    btw OUT: err
